note: schema.q:2:1 — N_NO_HORIZON: table posts: `sync public` has no horizon, so every row of every group a device holds reaches it and stays; a device that holds many groups, or a public table that grows, pays for all of it at every cold start; measure what it costs with `check --residency`
  rewrite: sync public last 500 by .id
  guide: sync
note: schema.q:9:3 — N_MAINTAINED_COLUMN_STREAM: posts: each contributing commit logs and streams the whole parent image per destination partition, coalesced once per row; a 4,000-byte parent costs every holder about 4 KB per change
  rewrite: use a column when readers want the count with the row; for a large row or a counter changing far more often than it is read, use a view with online only
  guide: maintains
